! pw.in template for the E3-QE/MACE LiFePO4 audit (PBE+U, Fe 3d, U=5.3 eV).
! Per Max's review: QEBackendConfig cannot yet emit the HUBBARD card, so
! LiFePO4 (the only one of the six E3 materials needing DFT+U) goes through
! this pw_template instead of the generated-input path. When pw_template is
! set, qe.py IGNORES ecutwfc_ry/ecutrho_ry/occupations/smearing/degauss_ry/
! extra_control/extra_system/extra_electrons from the YAML -- every one of
! those values must live in this file instead (see
! examples/active_learning/e3_qe_mace_lux_lifepo4.yaml).
!
! Python str.format() slots filled by qe.py:
!   {nat}        — number of atoms
!   {natoms}     — alias for {nat}
!   {ntyp}       — number of atomic species
!   {pseudo_dir} — absolute path to UPF directory
!   {prefix}     — pwscf prefix
!   {outdir}     — scratch dir for wavefunctions/charge
!
! The backend AUTO-APPENDS these structure-dependent cards after this file:
!   ATOMIC_SPECIES, CELL_PARAMETERS angstrom, ATOMIC_POSITIONS angstrom,
!   K_POINTS automatic   (k-mesh from qe.kpts / qe.koffset in the YAML --
!   kpts is NOT ignored when pw_template is set; e3_qe_mace_lux_lifepo4.yaml
!   pins it to [2, 4, 8] for the 112-atom 2x2x1 olivine supercell, per Max).
!
! Species are sorted alphabetically by qe.py before this template is filled:
!   LiFePO4 -> Fe (1), Li (2), O (3), P (4). starting_magnetization(1) below
!   is therefore Fe's, NOT an arbitrary index -- re-check this ordering if
!   the formula or backend's species-sorting rule ever changes.
!
! Pseudopotentials: SSSP 1.3.0 PBE-efficiency (Materials Cloud, DOI
! 10.24435/materialscloud:1r-4m). Record the SHA-256 of the Fe/Li/O/P UPFs
! actually used in E3_QE_RUN_DIR before a real run (not yet automated --
! see examples/active_learning/README.md "QE scientific settings (Lux)").
!
! starting_magnetization(i) in QE is a FRACTION of species i's pseudopotential
! valence-electron count (Zval), not a raw muB value. Converted below from
! Max's muB targets (Fe 5 muB, all other species 0.6 muB) using the standard
! SSSP-efficiency PSlibrary PAW Zval for each element (Fe=16, Li=3, O=6,
! P=5) -- TODO: confirm these four Zval numbers against the header of the
! ACTUAL UPF files once sourced (`grep z_valence *.UPF`); they were not
! re-derived from a located pseudopotential in this pass.
!   Fe: 5.0   / 16 = 0.3125
!   Li: 0.6   / 3  = 0.2
!   O:  0.6   / 6  = 0.1
!   P:  0.6   / 5  = 0.12

&CONTROL
  calculation   = 'scf'
  prefix        = '{prefix}'
  outdir        = '{outdir}'
  pseudo_dir    = '{pseudo_dir}'
  verbosity     = 'high'
  tprnfor       = .true.
  tstress       = .true.
  etot_conv_thr = 1.0d-5
  forc_conv_thr = 1.0d-4
  nstep         = 1
/

&SYSTEM
  ibrav               = 0
  nat                 = {nat}
  ntyp                = {ntyp}
  ecutwfc             = 90.0
  ecutrho             = 720.0
  occupations         = 'smearing'
  smearing            = 'gaussian'
  degauss             = 0.0037
  nspin               = 2
  starting_magnetization(1) = 0.3125
  starting_magnetization(2) = 0.2
  starting_magnetization(3) = 0.1
  starting_magnetization(4) = 0.12
/

&ELECTRONS
  conv_thr         = 1.0d-8
  mixing_beta      = 0.3
  electron_maxstep = 150
/

HUBBARD {{atomic}}
U Fe-3d 5.3
